('RPI-003','RPI','Number local LN policies developed or strengthened','Number',null,null,'Beneficiaries & Stakeholders','Improved national and sub-national policy climate for literacy and numeracy','LE, PA','Adv Goal 2','2022-2025: 8 Perbup L(N), 1 Draft Perwali, Inclusion of FLN in 13 district RPJMD 2025-2029','Policy and Advocacy (PA)'),
('RPI-004','RPI','Number of publications, citation and reference (annual)','Number',null,null,'Beneficiaries & Stakeholders','Tanoto Foundation serves as a thought and catalytic leader for human capital development within the social ecosystem','PA','Comms',null,'Policy and Advocacy (PA)'),
('RPI-005','RPI','Number of high-level forum on national or regional level with TF representation as a speaker bringing advocacy agenda (annual)','Number',null,null,'Beneficiaries & Stakeholders','Tanoto Foundation serves as a thought and catalytic leader for human capital development within the social ecosystem','PA','Comms',null,'Policy and Advocacy (PA)'),
('RPI-006','RPI','Number of reach harnessed from media (annual)','Number',null,null,'Beneficiaries & Stakeholders','Tanoto Foundation serves as a thought and catalytic leader for human capital development within the social ecosystem','PA','Comms',null,'Policy and Advocacy (PA)'),
('RPI-007','RPI','Successful implementation and ownership building for key grants Frequency coordination with key regional stakeholder','Percent',null,null,'Beneficiaries & Stakeholders','Strengthened institutions, policies, and people related to national stunting reduction initiatives','LE, PA','SINERGI, ALPHA, PANDAI','at least 1x meeting for each intervened district with local government top leaders (Bupati, or Sekda/ Asisten/Head of Bappeda) to report on progress for ownership building','Maternal and Child Health & Nutrition (MCHN)'),
('RPI-008','RPI','Successful implementation and ownership building for Stunting 2.0 Level of engagement with local government in program implementation','Percent',null,null,'Beneficiaries & Stakeholders','70% of partner districts have the capacity to do the stunting reduction program','LE','Stunting 2.0','- 30%: TA to government with IPs at provincial and district level (3x per year per district, total 27x) - 30%: Bi-annual joint monitoring (2x per year per district, total 18x) Join monitoring for KPP, Planning and Budgeting, Data Decision Making/POPS - 40%: Bi- annual Report of progress and ownership building of the local government (2x per year per district, total 18x) Bi Annual Report of Progress = Twice a year Reporting to the local government Ownership Building = Advocacy or Coordinating with the local government Formula TA = (Actual/27)*30% Bi Annual Join Monitoring = (Actual/18)*30% Bi Annual Report of Progress and Ownership Building = (Actual/18)*40%','Maternal and Child Health & Nutrition (MCHN)'),
('RPI-009','RPI','Percentage of data system (operational POPS) at village level established and data collected/updated','Percent',null,null,'Beneficiaries & Stakeholders','70% of partner districts have the capacity to do the stunting reduction program','LE','Stunting 2.0','Milestones, average progress in 18 villages: 1. operationalized to each village (2026) 30% 2. data collected - completed by May - (2026) 40% 3. data updated - monthly updated up to November - (2026) 30% formula: 1. (village that have operasionalized/18)*30% 2. (village with data collected/18)*40% 3. (village with data updated/18)*30% 2027 1. data utilized and used for decision making (2027) 2. data system sustained through budget/policy (2028-2030)','Maternal and Child Health & Nutrition (MCHN)'),
('RPI-010','RPI','Number of Rumah Anak SIGAP as CoE','Number',null,null,'Beneficiaries & Stakeholders','80% children in our centers developmentally on-track according to CREDI','LE','RAS','Criteria of CoE: to achieve 3 out 5 deliverables: - 70% parents has 85% attendance rate (6 out of 7 visits) (2026) - score of quality services >75 (2026) - standardize facilities (2026) - have cost effective delivery (2027) - capacity per center 50 dyad (2027)','Early Childhood Education and Development (ECED)'),
('RPI-011','RPI','Number local innovation facilitated by Rumah Anak SIGAP Facilitators','Number',null,null,'Beneficiaries & Stakeholders','80% children in our centers developmentally on-track according to CREDI','LE','RAS','Local innovation to improve parenting and early stimulation for 0-3yo child. Only for Kutai kartanegara.','Early Childhood Education and Development (ECED)'),
('RPI-012','RPI','Number of new Rumah Anak SIGAP built','Number',null,null,'Beneficiaries & Stakeholders','80% children in our centers developmentally on-track according to CREDI','LE','RAS','2026: 5 centres to be built in Medan using TF funding. Programme implementation will start in 2027 2027: 10 centers to be built and operationalize using TF funding (5 centers start to operate in Medan, 5 centers to be built in other region - TBC) 2030 : 25 centers to be built and operationalize using catalytic funding (by SPP = 12 RAS centers, and by LE= 13 RAS centers)','Early Childhood Education and Development (ECED)'),
('RPI-013','RPI','Successful pre and pilot implementation Regional: Level of engagement with local government in program implementation','Percent',null,null,'Beneficiaries & Stakeholders','Improved national and sub-national policy climate for early stimulation and parenting','PA','SPRING','Criteria: -50%: Coordination meeting with District Government., Village Head, and Coordinator of Pustu and Posyandu (3x) -50%: To make sure there is a '' Readiness Letter/Form'' by District and Village Gov.','Early Childhood Education and Development (ECED)'),
('RPI-014','RPI','Percentage of new levers program progress and compliance to program design as planned in 2026','Percent',null,null,'Beneficiaries & Stakeholders','4 levers shows the evidence of effective improvements in literacy and numeracy','LE','New Levers: DDSL, Numeracy Parent, Numeracy Teacher, PANDAI - Structured Pedagogy, PANDAI - DD Affirmative Action w. Digital Assessment','Criteria, to achieve all of this deliverables: a) Fidelity'||chr(59)||' attendance rate of participants (40%) --> For total 8 district - Numeracy Teacher -> participants in training > 80% (training conducted in 2026), DISTRICT: Karo, Siak, Kendal, Paser (4) - Numeracy Parent -> participants in socialization >40% (socialization conducted in 2026), DISTRICT: Karo, Siak, Kendal, Paser (4) - Formula: (x/8*40%) b) Advocacy'||chr(59)||' meeting progress with government and or joint monitoring 2x (30%) --> For total 17 district - DDSL -> DISTRICT: Nias (1) - Numeracy Teacher -> DISTRICT: Karo, Siak, Kendal, Paser (4), will be held around Sep/Oct - Numeracy Parent -> DISTRICT: Karo, Siak, Kendal, Paser (4), will be held around Sep/Oct - PANDAI Structured Pedagogy -> DISTRICT: Medan, Pematangsiantar, Batanghari, Tegal (4) - PANDAI DD Affirmative Action w. Digital Assessment -> DISTRICT: Medan, Pematangsiantar, Batanghari, Tegal (4) - Formula: (x/18*30%) c) Implementation'||chr(59)||' all planned activities implemented (30%) --> For total 8 districts - Numeracy Teacher -> Mentoring I (Cycle 1 Mar 2026), Mentoring II (Cycle 1 May 2026), Mentoring III (Cycle 1 around Jun/ Jul 2026), ToT II (Cycle 2 around Aug 2026), RO II (Cycle 2 around Sep 2026), Mentoring I (Cycle 2 around Nov 2026), DISTRICT: Karo, Siak, Kendal, Paser (4) - Numeracy Parent -> Briefing PIC I (Cycle 1 Jan 2026), Socialization I (Cycle 1 Jan 2026), Blasting 21 Content (Cycle 1 Feb-Jul 2026), Briefing PIC II (Cycle 2 Aug 2026), Socialization II (Cycle 2 Sep/ Oct 2026), Blasting 12 Content (Cycle 2 Sep-Dec 2026, the remaining content will continue next year), DISTRICT: Karo, Siak, Kendal, Paser (4) - Formula: (x/8*30%) NB: A District is counted if all planned activities are completed in that district. 2030 target to be reduce to 4 as it will use higher level of indicator Total Formula: (x/8*40%) + (x/17*30%) + (x/8*30%)','Basic Education (BE)'),
('RPI-015','RPI','Number of local innovation adopted by schools or governments or private sectors (annual)','Number',null,null,'Beneficiaries & Stakeholders','31 districts sustain/scale the implementation of teaching & learning improvement programs','LE','PINTAR','- Local innovation to improve FLN initiated by PINTAR Facilitators. - Adopted: Local innovations that are supported through external funding sources (other than TF) for the implementation or scale-up of the Fasda project Adoption is counted as 1 innovation if at least one criterion is met'||chr(59)||' regardless of how many criteria are fulfilled. The assessment covers innovation projects during 2023-2025. Adoption criteria: - Receives of catalytic funding from local goverment or government-recommended organizations - Use of Fasda resources (facilitators and or their modules) - Use or replication of Fasda project outputs/ products (e.g. The pop-up book product of a Fasda project group was adopted by another group without additional training)','Basic Education (BE)'),
('RPI-016','RPI','Number of partner districts with a sustained monitoring system (i.e., all indicators above are fulfilled)','Number','Cummulative',null,'Beneficiaries & Stakeholders','Improved national and sub-national policy climate for literacy and numeracy: APS-like monitoring system on school quality is adapted by national government','LE','APS','-Successfull transfer in Kendal, Karo, and Dumai Criteria for Siak and Kubar, fullfill 5 out of 5 deliverables: - Prototype developed and monitoring system team established - Implementation/ data collected - Policy commitment (SK/SE) - Budget allocated - Data utilized/analyzed for decision making','Basic Education (BE)'),
('RPI-017','RPI','Percentage of fellows who get exposure to field experience','Percent',null,null,'Beneficiaries & Stakeholders','Leaders contribute to​ the community and country','LDS','Fellowship','Numerator: number of fellows who get exposure to field experience meeting the indicators below: 25%: Exposure to government 25%: Mentorship 1 time/quarter by RL 25%: Exposure > 3 TF projects 25%: Exposure to local network (Media, Local NGO, CSR, community movement) Denominator: total number of fellows','Leadership Development and Scholarship (LDS)'),
('RPI-018','RPI','Level of government engagement and maintenance.','Number',null,null,'Beneficiaries & Stakeholders','Government demonstrates enhanced capacity and financial commitment to improve human capital development','PA','GEA','Criteria: - 10%: MoU active/issued - 10%: PKS active/issued - 20%: Foundation level Meetings w Regional high level officials (bupati atau wakil/walikota atau wakil/ Sekda atau Kepala Bappeda/ Kepala OPD) - 20%: Gov high level officials attended TF events - 20%: Recognitions from government (Awards, documentation of statements, letters) - 20%: Zero MoU/PKS termination due to dispute (X/27*10%)+(X/39*10%)+(X/27*20%)+(X/27*20%)+(X/27*20%)+(X/27*20%)','Policy and Advocacy (PA)'),
('RPI-019','RPI','Number of Public advocacy campaign executed on the national and subnational level','Number',null,null,'Beneficiaries & Stakeholders','Tanoto Foundation serves as a thought and catalytic leader for human capital development within the social ecosystem','PA','Comms','- Orchestrate public advocacy campaign involving national & regional comms team around TF advocacy goals in place by utilizing necessary public advocacy tools (op-ed, podcast, social media, event, community activation, FGD, and other communications initiatives) - 2026: 1 PES, 1 LN public advocacy campaign','Policy and Advocacy (PA)'),
('RPI-020','RPI','Zero major audit findings','Number',null,null,'Learning & Growth','Operation excellence & sustainable growth','All','All',null,null),
('RPI-021','RPI','Efficient budget absorption: LE cost saving','Number',null,null,'Learning & Growth','Operation excellence & sustainable growth','FATLC','FATLC',null,null),
('RPI-022','RPI','Number of CI projects completed and operationalized (annual)','Number',null,null,'Learning & Growth','Operation excellence & sustainable growth','SPP','KM','2 per regional ( 1 for CI Program and 1 for CI Support)',null),
('RPI-023','RPI','Key succession leadership in-place and key subject-matter expertise available','Number',null,null,'Learning & Growth','Operation excellence & sustainable growth','All','HR','Regional lead identified and consulted with LE Jakarta: - 1 successor - 1 BE specialist - 1 ECED specialist',null)
